\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Overview of DCD. A frozen SAM ViT-L encoder is adapted with block-internal Adapter-I modules and block-external Adapter-E features. The prompt-free mask decoder updates four learnable mask tokens with a Two-way Transformer and fuses the Adapter-E features through Adapter-F: the features from all 24 blocks are pooled, softmax-weighted, projected, and added to the upsampled decoder feature. Stage-1 produces four coarse masks, whose gating scores rank the candidate descriptors; Stage-2 then refines the ranked candidates with dense, topology, and role-specific losses. At inference, gating only determines the candidate order, and DCD always deploys the same ranked slot (slot 3), with no test-time candidate selection or fusion. The head-fusion branch is used only during training. Predictions are resized to the input resolution and thresholded at 0.5.}}{2}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dcd_framework}{{2}{2}{Overview of DCD. A frozen SAM ViT-L encoder is adapted with block-internal Adapter-I modules and block-external Adapter-E features. The prompt-free mask decoder updates four learnable mask tokens with a Two-way Transformer and fuses the Adapter-E features through Adapter-F: the features from all 24 blocks are pooled, softmax-weighted, projected, and added to the upsampled decoder feature. Stage-1 produces four coarse masks, whose gating scores rank the candidate descriptors; Stage-2 then refines the ranked candidates with dense, topology, and role-specific losses. At inference, gating only determines the candidate order, and DCD always deploys the same ranked slot (slot 3), with no test-time candidate selection or fusion. The head-fusion branch is used only during training. Predictions are resized to the input resolution and thresholded at 0.5}{figure.caption.2}{}}
\newlabel{fig:dcd_framework@cref}{{[figure][2][]2}{[1][1][]2}{}{}{}}
